        extracted into one shared implementation. Extracted a shared
        _with_hard_timeout($seconds, $label, $coderef) into
        D2TG::Config; both packages now call it, each passing its own
        exact pre-extraction die-message prefix ("D2TG::Telegram
        <method>" / "D2TG::Download::download_file") so both call
        sites' wording is unchanged. Matches the established
        shift_flag_value (TGT-072) / _classify_store_error (TGT-167) /
        _format_forwarded_sender (TGT-170) /
        _validate_reply_to_message_id (TGT-171) /
        resolve_alias_dir_or_die (TGT-172) precedent, this time
        cross-package. No behavioral change - verified via a
        before/after full-suite diff (Files=131, Tests=1259 both
        times) and 100% statement+subroutine coverage on
        D2TG::Config.pm, D2TG::Telegram.pm, and D2TG::Download.pm.

