1.18  2026-09-09
      - RELIABILITY FIX (TGT-147, found via scheduled hourly bug hunt
        JOB-003, a real regression this same session's own earlier
        TGT-140 introduced): d2 tg.status's STALE_THRESHOLD_SECONDS
        (a fixed 1200s literal) never got updated when TGT-140 changed
        D2TG::Transcribe's per-tier timeout from a flat 300s to a
        duration-scaled value up to 3600s - a healthy, still-
        transcribing poller working through a long voice note's retry
        ladder could be falsely reported STALE after only 20 minutes,
        up to 9x below the new real worst case (up to 3 hours). Now
        derived directly from D2TG::Transcribe's own $TIMEOUT_CEILING
        and @MODEL_TIERS constants (currently 14400s/4h) instead of a
        re-typed literal, so the two can never silently drift apart
        again. Codex caught a real follow-up gap in the fix's own
        tests (hard-coded to the literal 14400 instead of computing it
        from the same source constants) - fixed.

